# The --skip-to-area and --skip-to-cutscene row table
# (tests/harness/check_skip_targets.sh).
#
# --skip-to-area: one row per sub-area, every sub-area 1..N-1 of the 17
# multi-area levels (38), each entered by one area-0 portal. A row passes
# when its run prints the skip's release line ("[skip-to-level] level
# playable") carrying every expect token, the level and area words
# (0x8006C5BC, 0x8006C5C8) read back from RAM at release: game.state 13 seen
# after the EnterSubArea call, then gameplay live in the target area. It
# fails when the run prints the fail-safe line. Level 31 arrives in the
# first-visit speech (game.state 1), which the area-0 portal refuses; its
# rows replay a movie that dismisses it. frames is the run's VBL limit
# (releases measured at VBL 1686, 1900 for level 31).
#
# --skip-to-cutscene: one row per story cutscene (19). The release line
# carries the row's name, the cutscene index 0x8006EDD8 and currentLevel
# 0x8006C5BC (the cutscene id) read back from RAM at release: game.state 6
# with the row's index after the row's WarpToLevel(6, id) call. Chain rows
# (75, 76 after 61; 70, 71, 73 after 69) release when the game's own chain
# reaches them. Levels 37 and 47 open a speech (game.state 1) before their
# first live tick; their rows replay a movie whose Cross taps dismiss it and
# end before the call (a Cross press during playback ends a cutscene).
#
# Expect tokens match the release line; `log:TEXT`, `log:A>>B` and
# `!log:TEXT` match the whole log (`~` for a space; forms in
# tests/harness/check_skip_targets.sh). Row 61 commits New Game from the title's
# idle sub-state instead of sub-state 19, whose phase 0 teardown
# func_title_8007C268 clears interrupt callback line 7; the skip calls that
# teardown before the commit. The row's log tokens require the clear
# before the loading overlay replaces the title and no callback dispatch to
# an address without a compiled body.
#
# name | args                                                                                              | frames | expect
