# Windowed --skip-to-level row (mode:windowed, forms in
# tests/harness/check_skip_targets.sh). The skip holds presents back while
# the level loads; the first present after the release must not carry the
# load and demo screens' 2D over the level: no OVERLAY_CARRY_MAX line, a
# "held presents=" line, and the probe line reads mismatch=0. The release
# comes on the fade-in's first tick, whose presents hold no 2D (carry_n=0,
# scene_n=0); carry_f>=1030 takes the probe line at the first present
# after the fade-in (f=1030, VBL 1604), where the level's 2D and the scene
# are both live. The entry rows below take it there too.
# name                         | args                         | frames | expect
s3-haunted-tomb-first-present  | --skip-to-level haunted_tomb | 2200   | mode:windowed carry_f>=1030

# Windowed --skip-to-level entry rows (mode:windowed). Every level enters
# through game.state 5 (loading image), 3 (fade-in from black, VBL 1570 to
# 1603 here), then 0, or 1 in the ten levels that open on a first-visit
# speech, whose camera move into the speaker runs from VBL 1604 before the
# speech waits for a button. The release must come at the fade-in's first
# tick, so the fade-in and the camera move are presented: vbl<=1570. A
# release that waits for game.state 0 never comes in a speech level before
# the fail-safe (VBL 4574) and fails the row. icy_peak opens in gameplay
# (release at 1604 on game.state 0, 1570 on the fade-in).
# name                         | args                          | frames | expect
s3-frozen-altars-speech-entry  | --skip-to-level frozen_altars | 1800   | mode:windowed vbl<=1570 carry_f>=1030
s3-crawdad-farm-speech-entry   | --skip-to-level crawdad_farm  | 1800   | mode:windowed vbl<=1570 carry_f>=1030
s3-icy-peak-entry              | --skip-to-level icy_peak      | 1800   | mode:windowed vbl<=1604 carry_f>=1030
